# Recorded line audio, capture logs and run outputs. Deliberately untracked:
# a single hardware session is hundreds of megabytes, and the write-ups in
# docs/eicon_adsp_firmware_analysis.md carry the conclusions.
artifacts/

# Built by `make -C tools/adsp2181emu`, not by anything at the top level.
*.dylib
*.so
*.o
tools/adsp2181emu/eicon_adsp_run
tools/adsp2181emu/adsp2181_core_test
# tools/adsp2181emu/dasm/dasm is committed on purpose: a 42 KB arm64 build of
# the MAME disassembler wrapper, kept so a fresh checkout can disassemble
# without a C++ build. Rebuild it with the command in the README if you are on
# another architecture.

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.dSYM/
.DS_Store

# The vendored driver ships the same firmware images as docs/firmware/, which
# is already tracked. Verified byte-identical (all 54 files, 60 MB), so the
# copy is excluded rather than doubling the repository for no new information.
docs/divas4linux-master/firmware/

# The recovered 109-era directory: 34 of its 45 files are byte-identical to
# docs/firmware/. The eleven that genuinely differ are tracked separately in
# docs/firmware/build-109/, so the directory itself is kept locally as the
# unpacked original and not committed.
docs/firmware/firmware/

# The recovered DIVA Server for OS/2 6.03e package. Only its card firmware --
# the MIPS protocol images, the FPGA bitstream and the DSP combifile -- is
# tracked, plus CONTENT.TXT, which is what docs/older_firmware_comparison.md
# cites for the package's identity and date. The OS/2 drivers, CAPI DLLs,
# utilities and the servod PDF are host-side software that nothing here loads;
# they stay local.
docs/firmware/divase/*
!docs/firmware/divase/*.BIT
!docs/firmware/divase/*.BIN
!docs/firmware/divase/TE_*.PM
!docs/firmware/divase/TE_*.QM[0-3]
!docs/firmware/divase/TE_*.SM
!docs/firmware/divase/CONTENT.TXT

# Local overrides for ./run profiles: registrar host, credentials, an
# interpreter somewhere other than /tmp/eicon-venv. Same shape as
# profiles.toml, overlaid a table at a time.
profiles.local.toml
